      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIEm">III Em</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="191" ed="#liebermann"/>[V.] Et nemo barganniet uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#IIIEm_5.lnote.oe.a"/> ignotum pecus recipiat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#IIIEm_5.lnote.oe.b"/>, qui non habeat testimonium summi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#IIIEm_5.lnote.oe.c"/> prepositi uel sacerdotis uel hordarii<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIIEm_5.lnote.oe.5"/> uel portireue.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="14" ed="#robertson"/>Et nemo barganniet vel ignotum pecus recipiat qui non habeat testimonium summi praepositi vel sacerdotis vel hordarii<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IIIEm_5.robnote.fn.5"/> vel portirevae.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIIEm_5.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="15" ed="#robertson"/>And no-one shall make a purchase or receive strange cattle unless he has as witness the high-reeve or the priest or the treasurer or the town-reeve<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIIEm_5.robnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="191"><ref target="clause:IIAs_10">II As 10</ref>; <ref target="clause:IIAs_12">II As 12</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II As. 10. 12</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Hu_4">Hu 4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="361"><label>based on</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_23">II Cn 23–24</ref> <quote>their subject is covered by II Cn 23 – 24, itself based on ?I Ew 1:2, II As 10, 12, ?III Em 5</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only; no German translation in Liebermann. Liebermann compares II As 10, 12.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIEm_5.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">191</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ordalii <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ordalii <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIEm_5.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ <hi rend="italic">nan man ne ceapige ne onfó</hi> (oder <hi rend="italic">underfó</hi>) <hi rend="italic">uncuð yrfe</hi> (oder <hi rend="italic">feoh?</hi>), <hi rend="italic">þe næbbe heahgerefan gewitnesse oððe mæssepreostes oððe horderes oððe portgerefan</hi> lautete Or. laut II As 10. 12. Hu 4, wo dies benutzt scheint</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ <hi rend="italic">nan man ne ceapige ne onfó</hi> (or <hi rend="italic">underfó</hi>) <hi rend="italic">uncuð yrfe</hi> (or <hi rend="italic">feoh?</hi>), <hi rend="italic">þe næbbe heahgerefan gewitnesse oððe mæssepreostes oððe horderes oððe portgerefan</hi> was the reading of the original, according to II As 10. 12. Hu 4, where this seems to have been used</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIEm_5.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Verbot, unbekannte, daher verdächtige, Fahrhabe zu übernehmen, ist vom Erhandeln her hier allgemeiner ausgedehnt. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Handel 8a; Kaufzeugen 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The prohibition on taking over unknown, and therefore suspect, chattels is here extended from acquisition by purchase to a more general scope. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Handel 8a; Kaufzeugen 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIEm_5.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">130</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl: heahgerefa</hi> 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl: heahgerefa</hi> 3</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIEm_5.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">299</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II As. 10; 12.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIEm_5.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">299</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hordarii</hi> (<hi rend="italic">ordalii</hi>) <hi rend="italic">vel portirevae</hi>, <hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> A.S. <hi rend="italic">horderes oððe portgerefan</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIIEm_5.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">14</biblScope></bibl><label>hordarii</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ordalii</hi> M, Hk, Br.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
